e exposure from the Emirates Astronomical Observatory are read V-G-R. That's a call sign for the Voyager 1 spacecraft currently in interstellar space some 26 billion kilometers away. How long did it take the message to reach humanity's most distant interstellar spacecraft ? Traveling at the speed of light, the answer is one day. In fact, the Voyager 1 spacecraft was confirmed to reach its one light-day distance milestone on November 18, at 10:16:07 UTC, nearly 50 years after launch in 1977. For extra credit, fans of math can calculate that at one light-day per 50 years, Voyager 1 will reach its one light-year (365 light-days) distance milestone in about 18,250 years.","img":"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/IMG_4364N_Kyriazis.jpg?w=1400&fit=clip","by":"Apostolos Kyriazis","video":false},"tle":["1 25544U 98067A   26324.49484038  .00009536  00000+0  17778-3 0  9992","2 25544  51.6319 246.5768 0007409  46.6569 313.5036 15.49509114595987"],"passes":[{"start":"2026-11-21T17:36:05Z","end":"2026-11-21T17:40:40Z","top":"2026-11-21T17:39:26Z","max":89,"from":["W","西"],"to":["E","東"],"mins":5},{"start":"2026-11-21T19:12:52Z","end":"2026-11-21T19:13:37Z","top":"2026-11-21T19:16:12Z","max":68,"from":["W","西"],"to":["W","西"],"mins":1},{"start":"2026-11-22T16:48:08Z","end":"2026-11-22T16:54:50Z","top":"2026-11-22T16:51:28Z","max":84,"from":["W","西"],"to":["E","東"],"mins":7},{"start":"2026-11-22T18:24:55Z","end":"2026-11-22T18:27:44Z","top":"2026-11-22T18:28:16Z","max":81,"from":["W","西"],"to":["W","西"],"mins":3},{"start":"2026-11-23T17:36:57Z","end":"2026-11-23T17:41:32Z","top":"2026-11-23T17:40:18Z","max":90,"from":["W","西"],"to":["E","東"],"mins":5},{"start":"2026-11-23T19:13:46Z","end":"2026-11-23T19:14:28Z","top":"2026-11-23T19:16:56Z","max":41,"from":["W","西"],"to":["W","西"],"mins":1},{"start":"2026-11-24T16:48:57Z","end":"2026-11-24T16:55:39Z","top":"2026-11-24T16:52:18Z","max":87,"from":["W","西"],"to":["E","東"],"mins":7